# What of the repository enters the renderer's build context.
#
# It is an allow-list, and it has to be: the root of a working checkout
# carries a Rust build directory of hundreds of gigabytes, and a deny-list
# that forgot one of them would send it all to the daemon before the first
# instruction ran.
#
# BuildKit reads this file because it sits beside the Dockerfile and
# carries its name; the repository root keeps no `.dockerignore` of its
# own, so the site package stays self-contained and no other build in the
# tree inherits these rules (R-10).

# Nothing, unless named below.
**

# ── The Rust workspace `cargo build -p vibe-cli` resolves ──────────────
# Every member, plus what the manifest path-depends on and what the
# production code embeds at compile time.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/**
!xtask/**
!formats/**
!schemas/**
!vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.ai-native/**

# ── The site package ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
!vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/**

# ── The checkout the render reads as its second source ─────────────────
# The project's own card and text, the specifications its citations
# resolve against, and the documentation packages it carries in tree —
# which is exactly what `feed::host_feed` hashes and renders. The walk
# that finds those packages reads a `vibe.toml` per slot, so every slot's
# manifest comes along and nothing else of the other packages does.
!vibe.toml
!vibe.lock
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!vibevm/vibespecs/**
!vibevm/vibepacks/**/vibe.toml
!vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.core/**

# ── And never, whatever named it back ──────────────────────────────────
# Build output, installed dependencies and version-control state: all
# reproducible, all large, none of it an input.
#
# The site package's output directories are written out in full rather
# than matched by name anywhere: `server` and `dist` are also the names of
# two ordinary source directories in this tree, and a pattern that read
# them as build output would delete half a crate from the context and
# fail the compile three minutes later with a missing module.
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.git
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/site/dist
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/site/dist-embedded
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/site/server
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/site/server-embedded
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/site/test-results
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/test-results
vibevm/vibepacks/org.vibevm.doc/web/v1.0.0/tmp
